p621:record_40631d05 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_4a078711,
        p621:source_b6911bdd ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_2_part_2 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:1187746527099 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_73e571ab ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "The company “M3”, which owns the streaming service “More.tv”, was fined for two films: “Three Many Weddings” (Javier Ruiz Caldera, 2013) and “Blow Dry” (Paddy Breathnach, 2001), both labelled “16+”. According to the court, these films “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” among minors. The experts from Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, found eight scenes with such demonstration in the first title (the exact time codes are 00:56:57-00:58:20, 00:58:21-00:58:52, 01:00:12-01:01:33, 01:01:34-01:02:10, 01:02:11-01:03:29, 01:04:14-01:04:22, 01:06:19-01:06:34, 01:10:32-01:11:00). In the second title, the experts identified one scene (01:21:47-01:21:57), in which “two characters of the same sex (female) kissing in a sexual context.” The deputy general director of the company was also fined for the same content (see case 5-940/23)."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:17203,
        p621:201765 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2023"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "05-0583/2023" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:77 ;
    schema:identifier "record_40631d05" .

p621:record_40ba3590 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_b09d2613 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_3 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0052 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_12ce6d5e ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "An individual was fined for a 15-second TikTok video. The video showed the defendant “wearing headphones, glasses, and a black T-shirt — moving to music while text appeared on screen”. Although the court repeatedly stated that the text was central to the offence, its wording was not reproduced in the judgment. By the time police opened proceedings, the original TikTok post had already been deleted, but officers testified that the clip had spread to Telegram channels. The same individual was prosecuted at least 7 times for different TikTok videos."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:social_media_110 ;
    dataout:mentionedIn p621:mentioned_in_bc832cac ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-299/87/2025" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:77 ;
    schema:identifier "record_40ba3590" .

p621:record_4208b34f a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_cabde74d,
        p621:source_e1f15ffc ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_2_part_2 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:1027739048281 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_3acb5f54 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "The TV channel “TV Tsentr – Moscow” was fined for broadcasting the programme “The Nineties” (2016). According to the court, the episode “The beauty queens” demonstrated “non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” in the scene, in which two women embracing and kissing: “In 2009, the fifty-two-year-old world tennis star announced that she had found herself a new girlfriend [...] two years later, she said that, with the help of her beloved, she had overcome a terrible illness and proposed marriage. The women entered into a happy marriage...” Earlier, the TV channel's deputy director was also fined for broadcasting this programme (see case 05-1326/374/2024)."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:tv_programme_002 ;
    dataout:mentionedIn p621:mentioned_in_dec526af ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "05-0067/2025" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:77 ;
    schema:identifier "record_4208b34f" .

p621:record_4400eabf a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_792c4f49,
        p621:source_d3a5673e ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_3 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0077 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_e2b6564b ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "A VKontakte user was fined for publishing a picture of “two kissing women and symbols similar to those of the extremist organisation 'LGBT movement'” in 2019. The court described the picture as “two women standing next to each other, kissing in the courtyard of a residential building, covered with a cloth consisting of stripes placed on top in the order: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, purple.” The judicial expert concluded that the picture depicts positevely “non-traditional sexual relations (not between a man and a woman), [...] it is expressed visually (the viewer is shown that this is beautiful, aesthetically pleasing, and therefore good and acceptable); [...] sexual relations not between a man and a woman are presented as acceptable for public display, on par with heterosexual ones.” The exact picture is unknown. The same individual was fined five times on the same day by the same court for publishing pictures on VK. The media reported that the first-instance court imposed a 100,000 RUB fine for each case. The higher-instance court reduced the fine, but the amount is unknown."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:social_media_057 ;
