p621:record_83c3f5b7 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_da803add ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_4 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0082 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_6380dc99 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "An individual was fined for a profile on a website, which “advertised sex services”. According to the court, the textual and visual information in the profile is “unambiguously aimed at popularizing and promoting non-traditional sexual relations, including among minors, and may contribute to the emergence of interest in children and adolescents in non-traditional forms of sexual behavior.” The court mentioned that “the page contains information that [the defendant] is a person of non-traditional sexual orientation, that is, a transsexual.” The defendant explained that she identifies as a woman and provides sex services only to men, which “exludes non-traditionalism”."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:dating_profile_006 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2024"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "12-194/2024 (12-3666/2023)" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:23 ;
    schema:identifier "record_83c3f5b7" .

p621:record_843d29d7 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_05bc80b6,
        p621:source_b07cf90b ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_1 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0109 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_b78974f4 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "The admin of the VKontakte page “Overheard at the Bar-club 'Slivki' Kazan 18+” was fined for publishing photos “promoting same-sex sexual relations (men kissing in women's clothing)”, according to the court. The judge stated that the defendant “promoted the ideology of the LGBT movement on the Internet, which is used, among other things, to destroy traditional spiritual and moral values”, and that the photos were “aimed at uniting supporters and coordinating the activities of the LGBT movement.” In court, the defendant explained that the photos were taken at “a parody theatre club where men dress up in women's clothing.” When imposing the fine, the judge took into account a mitigating circumstance – the defendant's disability."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:social_media_041 ;
    dataout:mentionedIn p621:mentioned_in_c98220f6 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2024"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-205/2024" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:16 ;
    schema:identifier "record_843d29d7" .

p621:record_84701b32 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_430b0316 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_3 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0088 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_979047bb ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "An individual was fined for several Instagram posts that depicted two women kissing, embracing, and touching each other. The accompanying captions were: “This is an ad for my handbag with foxes”, “1 year V O, what a year it has been! Others don’t experience this much in five years. Thank you for making me happy,” as well as photographs labelled “Wife and wife.” Other posts showed the pair holding hands next to a white poster with wedding-ring illustrations and captions like “We have been together for 2 years. I love you,” “Three years! She came up with the name for this anniversary — Flirtovshchina© Thank you for being ebanuty [fucked up] together©,” and a photo of a couple embracing with the caption: “My little pumpkin, my sweet eclair, the syrup to my potatoes! Now you are also a woman 35+. Happy birthday.”"@en,
        "Пользовательница Инстаграма была оштрафована за несколько публикаций, на которых “представители женского пола, [...] целуются друг с другом, обнимаются, трогают друг друга за различные части тела”. Суд указал, что фотографии были подписаны так: “Это реклама моей сумочки с лисиками”, “1 год V О, что это был за год! Иным не удается столько пережить вместе за пять лет. Спасибо, что делаешь меня счастливой.” Также были дргуие фотографии: с “поцелуем в губы” и текстом “Жена и жена”; как пара держится за руки рядом с белым плакатом и изображениями обручальных колец с подписями “Нам 2 года. Я люблю тебя”, “Нам 3 года! Настя придумала название этой годовщине — Флиртовщина© Спасибо за being ebanuty вместе © V Ф”; как пара обнимается с подписью “Моя тыковка, любименький эклерчик, сиропчик к моей картошке! Теперь ты тоже женщина 35+ С днём рождения.”"@ru ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:social_media_042 ;
    dataout:mentionedIn p621:mentioned_in_5543ed92 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2024"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-1-460/2024" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:16 ;
    schema:identifier "record_84701b32" .

p621:record_84d23455 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_66eb045c ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_7 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0056 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_detention_00e26b3c,
        p621:pen_expulsion_be279a5b ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "A foreign individual from Tajikistan was prosecuted after police inspected his Telegram account and concluded that the content published there amounted to “propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations”. According to the inspection record, police found that the account was not only storing material but also advertising intimate services: the judgment states that the defendant presented himself as an “active bisexual” and offered “both heterosexual and homosexual services” through private messages on Telegram."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:social_media_064 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-92/2025" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:66 ;
    schema:identifier "record_84d23455" .

p621:record_867c80a6 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_9e1b507e,
        p621:source_e64a6933 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_2_part_2 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:official_0021 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_d4df9da7 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "The “Yandex” CEO Artem Savinovsky was fined for distributing ten films on the company's streaming service “Kinopoisk”: “Perfect Strangers” (Paolo Genovese, 2016), “Bridget Jones: The Edge of Reason” (Beeban Kidron, 2004), “Three Many Weddings” (Javier Ruiz Caldera, 2013), “Easy A” (Will Gluck, 2010), “Blow Dry” (Paddy Breathnach, 2001), “Compartment No. 6” (Juho Kuosmanen, 2021), “Greed” (Michael Winterbottom, 2019), “Green Book” (Peter Farrelly, 2018), “The Amusement Park” (the title translated from Russian, the exact film is unknown), and “Beanpole” (Kantemir Balagov, 2019). According to the court, these films “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” and should have been marked “18+” instead of “16+”. The court did not specify the exact scenes in these movies that constituted the violation. The company which owns the streaming service was fined earlier for the same titles (see case 05-1459/2023). This CEO was previously fined by the same court for four other titles (case 5-1020/23). "@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:17203,
