p621:record_9e7b5d6b a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_82ac980b ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_1 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:1222400011316 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_e07a8a94 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "The company “Elton John Krasnoyarsk”, which owns the queer club “Elton”, was fined for “propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences and sex change during [...] ‘drag queen shows’.” The police came to the club after a complaint was filed against it. During their visit, the police noticed that the drag show “featured male participants dressed as females [...] interacting with bar clients.” They also determined that “some same-sex visitors engaged in non-traditional sexual behaviour (hugging and kissing each other on the lips) [...] directed at an unspecified number of visitors present within the premises.” Among the pieces of evidence the court reviewed were security camera recordings inside the club, which were described as “male bar visitors hugging and kissing each other in front of the stage”, “a male figure dressed in women's clothing, a dress, a wig, and bright makeup, stands near the stage in front of the sofas, interacting with male visitors”, and “near the bar counter, two women are hugging and kissing each other on the lips.”"@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:queer_venue_003 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2024"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-160/2024" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:24 ;
    schema:identifier "record_9e7b5d6b" .

p621:record_9ff5e6f3 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_72881c92 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_3 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:official_0031 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_f004e300 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "The project manager at “Mangalib”, a platform for online comics and manga, was prosecuted for several publications. The publication in this case is the manga “Reincarnation Coliseum: The Weakest Skill Conquers the Strongest Women and Creates a Harem” (Harawata Saizou, 2022), which “depicted romantic and/or sexual relationships between female characters”. This individual was fined at least 12 times for different publications. The company “MangaLib” was also fined at least 12 times."@en,
        "Менеджер проектов “Мангалиб”, платформы онлайн-комиксов и манги, был привлечён к ответственности за несколько публикаций. Публикация в этом деле – “Реинкарнация в колизее” (Harawata Saizou, 2022), в которой “изображаются романтические и/или сексуальные отношения между лицами женского пола”. Это должностное лицо было оштрафовано за различные публикации не менее 12 раз. ООО “Мангалиб” также была оштрафована не менее 12 раз."@ru ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:comics_006 ;
    dataout:mentionedIn p621:mentioned_in_c345bae3 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "05-0681/374/2025" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:77 ;
    schema:identifier "record_9ff5e6f3" .

p621:record_a0028f26 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_29db7be4 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_2_part_2 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:1167847381130 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_4c6fa489 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "The online streaming platform “Okko” was fined for the film “Black Ghosts” (Andreas Marawell, 2015), labelled “16+”. The court mentioned the timecodes of four scenes, which “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and preferences” to minors: 00:11:10-00:12:57; 00:15:46-00:16:54; 01:33:41-01:35:07; 01:29:19-01:31:42. It is not specified what these scenes depicted. The deputy general director of the streaming platform was also fined for the same film (see case 5-2433/2025-162)."@en,
        "Стриминговая платформа “Окко” была оштрафована за фильм “Черные призраки” (Andreas Marawell, 2015) с маркировкой “16+”. Суд упомянул четыре тайм-кода сцен, “демонстрирующих нетрадиционные сексуальные отношения и (или) предпочтения” среди несовершеннолетних: 00:11:10-00:12:57; 00:15:46-00:16:54; 01:33:41-01:35:07; 01:29:19-01:31:42. В постановлении не уточняется, что именно было показано в этих сценах. Заместитель генерального директора “Окко” также была оштрафована за распространение этого фильма (см. дело 5-2433/2025-162)."@ru ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:487498 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-2518/2025-162" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:78 ;
    schema:identifier "record_a0028f26" .

p621:record_a0695ec6 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_9af9f1b8,
        p621:source_ceaef6b9 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_2_part_2 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:1167847381130 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_6b03d6d5 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "The online streaming platform “Okko” was fined for three TV-series, labelled “16+”, which “contained a demonstration of non-traditional sexual relations and preferences”. As the St. Petersburg courts press office stated, the TV series “Annika” (Nick Walker, 2021) contained dialogs “referencing to non-traditional sexual relations” in episodes 2, 5, and 6. In the episode 4, there was “even a demonstration in the form of a kiss”. In the series “The One and Only” (Moon Jung-min, 2021), there were “bad scenes where one woman gently strokes the hand of another”. And the series “My Dead Ex” (Drew Hancock, 2018) “was let down by [..] a character's coming out”."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:127008,
        p621:130273,
        p621:80840 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2023"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-253/2024" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:78 ;
    schema:identifier "record_a0695ec6" .

p621:record_a0fded80 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_778248ba ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_1 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0100 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_519d0ab1 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "An individual was fined for dressing in women’s clothing in a public place. The court interpreted that as “promoting non-traditional sexual relations by appearance and behaviour. [...] while in a public place, positioned himself as a female, was dressed in women's clothing, had makeup on his face, and had manicure on his fingernails. He thereby promoted non-traditional sexual relations and committed actions aimed at fostering non-traditional sexual attitudes, the attractiveness of non-traditional sexual relations, and a distorted idea of ​​the social equivalence of traditional and non-traditional sexual relations.” This individual was fined twice for wearing “women's clothing” (see aslo 5-415/2025)."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:public_action_007 ;
