p621:record_bae4a8d3 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_28574f92,
        p621:source_792c4f49 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_3 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0077 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_5faf36f4 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "A VKontakte user was fined for publishing a picture of “two women kissing in front of a flag with the symbols of the extremist organisation 'LGBT movement'” in 2019. The court described the picture as “in the foreground, two womem are shown facing each other in close proximity; in the background, a canvas is partially displayed, on which stripes are visible, the colors of which go from top to bottom - red, orange, yellow, green.” The judicial expert concluded that the picture depicts positevely “non-traditional sexual relations (not between a man and a woman), [...] it is expressed visually (the viewer is shown that this is beautiful, aesthetically pleasing, and therefore good and acceptable); [...] sexual relations not between a man and a woman are presented as acceptable for public display, on par with heterosexual ones.” The exact picture is unknown. The same individual was fined five times on the same day by the same court for publishing pictures on VK. The media reported that the first-instance court imposed a 100,000 RUB fine for each case. The higher-instance court reduced the fine, but the amount is unknown. "@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:social_media_053 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2024"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "12-2085/2024" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:77 ;
    schema:identifier "record_bae4a8d3" .

p621:record_bafdf4fa a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_4bb78b7c ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_3 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0091 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_11ac001c ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "A VKontakte user was fined for four videos published on her personal page in 2011. The court found these videos “extremist” and “containing signs of propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations or preferences related to the LGBT community”, because they depicted “kisses between a man and a man”. Another individual was fined by the same court for similar content (case 5-207/2025)."@en,
        "Пользовательница ВКонтакте была оштрафована за четыре видеозаписи, опубликованные на её личной странице в 2011 году. Суд указал, что эти видеозаписи “экстремистского содержания” и “содержат признаки пропаганды нетрадиционных сексуальных отношений или предпочтений, относящиеся к ЛГБТ сообществу”, поскольку они изображали “поцелуи между мужчиной и мужчиной”. Ещё одно физическое лицо было оштрафовано тем же судом за похожий контент (см. дело 5-207/2025)."@ru ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:social_media_075,
        p621:social_media_cf89cf45,
        p621:social_media_dc857f52,
        p621:social_media_edae7a73 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-222/2025" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:77 ;
    schema:identifier "record_bafdf4fa" .

p621:record_bb5601c1 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_dea237b5 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_3 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0065 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_e5b51f99 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "A VKontakte user was fined for publishing a meme, which the court described as “the presidents of the United States and Russia lying in the same bed, with the following dialogue: '[Name redacted] - Will you recognise [Address redacted, most likely Crimea] for sure? [Name redacted] - Of course, dear!'” According to the court, this photo “was aimed at promoting LGBT and non-traditional sexual orientation.” The exact image is unknown. The amount of the fine has been redacted from the court ruling. This individual was fined four times by the same judge on the same day for posting on VK."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:social_media_103 ;
    dataout:mentionedIn p621:mentioned_in_421931e3 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
