p621:record_f2235dda a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_bba05562 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_2_part_2 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:official_0019 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_570518d4 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "The deputy general director for content on the streaming service “Ivi” was fined for the films “Little Italy” (Donald Petrie, 2018), “Dr. T & the Women” (Robert Altman, 2000), “Love Is Love Is Love” (Eleanor Coppola, 2021), and “Beginners” (Mike Mills, 2011) with the age restriction label “16+”. The court mentioned that these films contained “scenes describing homosexual relationships between men and [...] women, as well as references to homosexual relationships” demonstrating “non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” among minors. It is not specified which scenes exactly constituted the violation. The company that owns the streaming service was also fined for the same films (case 05-0902/2023)."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:10763,
        p621:523773,
        p621:55347,
        p621:680590 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2023"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-1479/23" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:77 ;
    schema:identifier "record_f2235dda" .

p621:record_f264cb14 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_0eb41d17 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_3 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:1237700761539 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_e1ffb7e1 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "“MangaLib”, a platform for online comics and manga, was fined for publications on its website. The publication in this case is “The Great Snake’s Bride” (Fushiashikumo, 2021). From the court decision: “This material, represented by one volume of 26 chapters, tells the story of a girl forced to marry a Snake (a giant snake). Initially, the girl is afraid of her husband, but soon the Snake succeeds in winning the young wife's affections, after which the characters begin an intimate relationship. The material contains non-episodic depictions of non-traditional sexual relations, represented by several illustrations of a female character (the main character) with a beast-like creature (perceived as a snake) in a romantic and erotic context: kissing, hugging, sensual touching, and sexually explicit actions. Therefore, the presented manga [...] contains information promoting non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences due to the systematic distribution of materials with non-episodic depictions and/or descriptions of non-traditional sexual relations.” The court stated that “the information displayed can be classified as revealing signs of a socio-cultural threat to the national security of the Russian Federation in terms of the protection of traditional values, since it reveals signs of ideological and psychological influence on the recipient in the form of the imposition of a destructive ideology (propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations).” This is one of at least 12 cases in a serial persecution of “MangaLib”. The manager of “MangaLib” was also prosecuted at least 12 times for different publications."@en,
        "“Мангалиб”, платформа онлайн-комиксов и манги, оштрафована за публикации на сайте. Публикация в этом деле – “Девушка замужем за Змеем” (Fushiashikumo, 2021). Согласно суду “в данном материале, представленным 1 томом из 26 глав, повествуется девушке, вынужденной выйти замуж за Змея (персонаж является гигантской змеей). Поначалу девушка боится супруга, но вскоре Змею удается добиться расположения молодой жены, после чего персонажи вступают в интимную связь. Материал содержит неэпизодическое изображение нетрадиционных сексуальных отношений, представленное несколькими иллюстрациями лица женского пола (главной героиней) со звероподобным существом (воспринимается в качестве змеи) в романтичном и эротическом контексте: поцелуи, объятия, чувственные прикосновения, сексуально откровенные действия. Таким образом, представленная манга [...] содержит информацию, пропагандирующую нетрадиционные сексуальные отношения и (или) предпочтения в связи с наличием систематического распространения материалов с неэпизодическим изображением и (или) описанием нетрадиционных сексуальных отношений.” Суд также заявил, что информация в этой публикации “может быть квалифицирована как обнаруживающая признаки социокультурной угрозы национальной безопасности РФ в части, касающейся защиты традиционных ценностей, так как обнаруживает признаки идеологического и психологического воздействия на реципиента в виде насаждения деструктивной идеологии (пропаганды нетрадиционных сексуальных отношений).” Это одно из как минимум 12 дел против “Мангалиб”. Менеджер платформы также был оштрафован за различные публикации не менее 12 раз."@ru ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:comics_010 ;
    dataout:mentionedIn p621:mentioned_in_08881344,
        p621:mentioned_in_27517825,
        p621:mentioned_in_3abdf6e4,
        p621:mentioned_in_93fb0552 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "05-0675/2025" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:77 ;
    schema:identifier "record_f264cb14" .

p621:record_f2da15a6 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_792c4f49,
        p621:source_db7fc1a5 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_3 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0077 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_c7c61033 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "A VKontakte user was fined for publishing a picture of “two women on the backdrop of a flag, which is the symbol of the extremist organisation 'LGBT movement'” in 2019. The court described the content of the picture: “two women standing opposite each other in a public place against the backdrop of a flag consisting of six stripes, the colors of which, from top to bottom, are red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and purple; the women' faces are turned toward each other, their mouths open and their tongues sticking out.” The judicial expert concluded that the picture depicts positevely “non-traditional sexual relations (not between a man and a woman), [...] it is expressed visually (the viewer is shown that this is beautiful, aesthetically pleasing, and therefore good and acceptable); [...] sexual relations not between a man and a woman are presented as acceptable for public display, on par with heterosexual ones.” The exact picture is unknown. The same individual was fined five times on the same day by the same court for publishing pictures on VK. The media reported that the first-instance court imposed a 100,000 RUB fine for each case. The higher-instance court reduced the fine, but the amount is unknown."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:social_media_056 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2024"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "12-2088/2024" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:77 ;
    schema:identifier "record_f2da15a6" .

p621:record_f547a1bd a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_1217cd6a ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_4 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0060 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_34628e42 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "An individual was prosecuted for posting images on VKontakte. The image in question depicted two women kissing with the text “I now declare you husband and wife.” The judicial expert concluded that this image “contains psychological and linguistic signs of propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations, expressed in the dissemination of information and the performance of public actions aimed at the formation of non-traditional sexual attitudes, the attractiveness of non-traditional sexual relations, and a distorted idea of ​​the social equivalence of traditional and non-traditional sexual relations and preferences.” This case was initiated by the “Cyber ​​Squad” project of the public movement “People's Front for Russia”, which identifies potentially “destructive content” and submits complaints to authorities."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:social_media_086 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-409/2025" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:2 ;
    schema:identifier "record_f547a1bd" .

p621:record_f5b264b5 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_67dd81cb ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_2_part_2 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:official_0012 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_68c09d15 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "The editor-in-chief of the “KinoLiving” TV channel was fined after Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, found that the TV channel aired the series “Episodes” (David Crane and Jeffrey Klarik, 2011), which “contained information demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences expressed by a visual component: an image of sensual interaction between two persons of the same biological sex (female), prolonged kisses and caresses of two women.”"@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:31841 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2023"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-1000/23" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:77 ;
    schema:identifier "record_f5b264b5" .

p621:record_f5d119be a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_ec1ecc14 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_3 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:individual_0053 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_6a104226 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "A Moscow resident was fined for a VKontakte video titled “Red and anarcho skinheads fight straights until complete victory.” The court classified the upload as “LGBT propaganda” without explaining the video’s visual content, context, or date of origin. The video was uploaded over 10 years before the ruling, and it shows skinheads and anarchist gatherings. As in the parallel rulings (case 05-0719/2025), liability was based primarily on the title and public accessibility of the material rather than on any detailed analysis of what the recording actually depicted. The same individual was fined at least twice for different online content."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:social_media_098 ;
    dataout:mentionedIn p621:mentioned_in_104b90c4,
        p621:mentioned_in_760fd5ae ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2025"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-718/25" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:77 ;
    schema:identifier "record_f5d119be" .

p621:record_f5fabe03 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_0e689276,
        p621:source_b5477777 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_part_3 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:1187847039742 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_1dafe1b3 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "The TV channel “AIVA” was fined for airing the music video “Tak Krasivo” (“So Beautiful”) by Sergey Lazarev (2017). The court did not publish the text of the decision. According to the mass media, the protocol stated that the video “demonstrated interacting hands (caressing each other), the position of which as well as their individual characteristics (hair, shape of the nail plate, manicure, jewelry) show that they belong to two people of the same-sex, which can be potentially perceived as a tactile, sensual interaction of persons conveying their homosexual preferences”, and that the video communicates “that people in non-traditional sexual relationships are not only no different from representatives of heterosexual relationships, but their preferences, if not socially approved, are at least acceptable in society and equivalent to the union of a man and a woman.” The editor-in-chief of this TV channel was also fined 200,000 RUB for the same video, as the media reported. However, we could not obtain the corresponding court decision."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:P5_F9XreimI ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2023"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-1665/2023" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:78 ;
    schema:identifier "record_f5fabe03" .

p621:record_f7f20549 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_26982a73 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy p621:MonitoringDec2025 ;
    dataout:concernsLegalArticle law:article_6_21_2_part_2 ;
    dataout:hasDefendant p621:official_0029 ;
    dataout:hasPenalty p621:pen_fine_08e64d17 ;
    dataout:hasSnippet "The deputy director general of the streaming service “PREMIER” was fined for the films “Perfect Strangers” (Paolo Genovese, 2016) and “Blow Dry” (2001, Paddy Breathnach). According to the court, these films “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” among minors, because they were labelled “16+”. Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, identified eight scenes in the first film (00:58:46–00:59:09, 01:01:05–01:01:35, 01:01:36–01:03:50, 01:04:32–01:04:55, 01:05:56–01:06:35, 01:17:24–01:17:29, 01:17:40–01:20:40, 01:22:10–01:22:21) “demonstrating (or describing) homosexual relations between men, as well as references to homosexual relationships.” In the film “Blow Dry”, Roskomnadzor found the scene (01:21:45-01:22:01) with “two characters of the same sex (female) kissing in a sexual context.” Earlier, the company, which owns the streaming service, was fined for the same content (see case 05-1040/2023)."@en ;
    dataout:hasTriggerObject p621:17203,
        p621:381341 ;
    dataout:monitoredIncidentYear "2023"^^xsd:gYear ;
    dataout:monitoringRecordNumber "5-641/23" ;
    schema:addressRegion region:77 ;
    schema:identifier "record_f7f20549" .

p621:record_f85d4f78 a dataout:MonitoringRecord ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom p621:source_8e0b75dc ;
